ssbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAMOTO, SHIGERU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAMURA, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KINOSHITA, NOBUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OSHIDA, NORIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINGAI, AKIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, MASASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKASU, MASAKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANAI, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YASUDA, ORIE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Novel depsipeptide derivatives bearing piperazinone rings in the molecule, represented by general formula (1) wherein X1 is N(R4)-CO, N(R5)-CH2, CH2-CO, CH2-CH2, CH=CH, CH2-CH(OH) or CH(OH)-CH(OH); R1 is C5-C20 alkyl or alkoxy(C5-C15)alkyl(C1-C4); R2 to R5 are each hydrogen or C1-C6 alkyl; and A is (2), (3) or (4): -X2-CH(R11)-X3-CH(R12)-NH-R13. These derivatives exhibit apolipoprotein E production accelerating activities, thus being useful as remedies for nerve injury, dementia and hyperlipidemia.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur de nouveaux dérivés de depsipeptides comportant dans la molécule des noyaux de pipérazinone et représentés par la formule générale (1) dans laquelle X1 représente N(R4)-CO, N(R5)-CH2, CH2-CO, CH2-CH2, CH=CH, CH2-CH(OH) ou CH(OH)-CH(OH); R1 représente C5-C20 alkyle ou alcoxy(C5-C15)alkyle(C1-C4); R2 à R5 représentent chacun hydrogène ou C1-C6 alkyle; et A représente (2), (3) ou (4): -X2-CH(R11)-X3-CH(R12)-NH-R13. Ces dérivés présentent des activités accélérant la production de l'apolipoprotéine E, et peuvent être utilisés comme remèdes pour les lésions nerveuses, la démence et l'hyperlipidémie.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>